<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hogs estimate Wednesday 105,000-USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hogs estimate Wednesday 105,000-USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said Wednesday's est receipts 105,000, Wk ago 90,000, and Yr ago 101,000 head. Estimates include generally about 60 percent Carcass Base Hogs. Barrows and gilts traded $0.50 higher than mid-session Tuesday. Trade was slow to moderate for goood demand and moderate offerings. Top $53.00 per cwt.</p>
<p>				   Country		  Plants</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>220-260 lbs		    50.50 -51.50	   51.50 -52.50</p>
<p>few					 50.00		    51.00</p>
<p>limited interest few		  52.00		    53.00</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>260-280 lbs		    48.50 -51.50	   49.00 -52.50</p>
<p>US 2-4   43-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>280-300 lbs		    45.00 -50.00	   45.50 -51.00</p>
<p>Sows - generally steady. Top $49.50.</p>
<p>US 1-3 300-450 lbs.	  40.00 -42.00	   41.00 -43.00</p>
<p>450-500 lbs.		   42.00 -45.00	   43.00 -46.00</p>
<p>500 lbs. up		    45.00 -48.50	   46.00 -49.50</p>
<p>in line four under country and plants, the usda make correction on plants from $49.50 to $50.50.</p>
